BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  **The Myth of the First Bridge**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (  In the time before time, two villages stood on opposite banks of a great river. The Giver's vi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    llage had fertile soil but no water. The Keeper's village had abundant springs but barren la) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    nd.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (  One day, the Giver gathered three baskets of grain-not all she possessed, but enough to show g) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (    enuine faith. She cast them into the river, whispering, "May these multiply in good hands.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (  The River Spirit, seeing such trust, tripled the grain as it floated downstream. The Keeper re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (    ceived nine baskets at her shore.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (  The Keeper faced a choice: keep all the bounty, or honor the trust shown. She understood that ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    the Giver had kept some grain back-wise caution, not selfishness. The Keeper returned five b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    askets upstream, keeping four for her village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (  Both villages ate well that season. The Giver had given three and received five-a gain. The Ke) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    eper had received nine and kept four-also a gain. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  From this exchange grew understanding. In future seasons, they built a bridge where the grain ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    had floated. Trust, measured and reciprocated, became the stones of that bridge.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  The River Spirit smiled, for she knew: prosperity flows not from hoarding, but from the courag) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    e to share and the wisdom to return.) Tj ET
