BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a valley. Each possessed a magic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        al spring, but the springs were cursed: their waters only multiplied when shared with th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        e other village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      One day, Elder Mara from the East village filled her vessel halfway and carried it across ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        the valley. "I trust you with this water," she said to Elder Kael of the West. As she po) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        ured it into his fountain, the water tripled before their eyes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      Kael faced a choice. He could keep all the abundant water for himself, or honor Mara's tru) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        st. He remembered his grandmother's teaching: "When someone crosses the valley bearing g) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        ifts, send them home richer than they came, but not so poor that you suffer.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      Kael returned half of the multiplied water. Both villages prospered-Mara returned home wit) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        h more than she left, and Kael kept enough to flourish.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      The pattern continued, generation after generation. Those who returned too little found no) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (         one would trust them again. Those who returned too much left their own village thirsty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (         But those who balanced generosity with wisdom created an eternal cycle of abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
