BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      In the time before time, two villages stood on opposite banks of a great river. The Giver') Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        s village had fertile soil but no water. The Keeper's village had abundant springs but b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        arren land.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      One day, the Giver gathered three baskets of grain-not all she possessed, but enough to sh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        ow genuine faith. She cast them into the river, whispering, "May these multiply in good ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        hands.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      The River Spirit, seeing such trust, tripled the grain as it floated downstream. The Keepe) Tj ET
