BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    Myth: Long ago, two villages traded across a misty canyon where echoes distorted every messa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      ge. The Water-Bearer would call out numbers, but fog twisted the sounds-sometimes "three" ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      became "none," and "plenty" became "empty.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    One season, the Water-Bearer filled three vessels and sent them across. But the mist was thi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      ck, and the Keeper received nothing-or perhaps received much but the vessels appeared empt) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      y through the fog's illusion. Neither knew what truly happened.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    The Water-Bearer, seeing no return, felt abandoned. The Keeper, receiving nothing, had nothi) Tj ET
